{"name":"June Day","hex":"#ffe182","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"june","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To rush."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/june"},{"term":"day","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-5 language code for Land Dayak languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is above the horizon and it lights the sky.","A period of time equal or almost equal to a full day-night cycle, being 24 hours long."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/day"}],"entries":[{"title":"June","blocks":[{"text":"June is the sixth month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars—the latter the most widely used calendar in the world. Its length is 30 days. June succeeds May and precedes July. This month marks the start of summer in the Northern Hemisphere and contains the summer solstice, which is the day with the most daylight hours. In the Southern Hemisphere, June is the start of winter and contains the winter solstice, the day with the fewest hours of daylight out of the year."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Statue_de_Junon%2C_Louvre%2C_Ma_485%2C_trois_quarts.JPG/330px-Statue_de_Junon%2C_Louvre%2C_Ma_485%2C_trois_quarts.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/June","wikidata":"Q120"},{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a day passes at a given location it experiences morning, afternoon, evening, and night. This daily cycle drives circadian rhythms in many organisms, which are vital to many life processes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day","wikidata":"Q573"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Chronography_of_354_Mensis_Iunius.png/330px-Chronography_of_354_Mensis_Iunius.png?utm_sou